(BAS2-53: the manual's open-with-treating example: the sentinel filename is substituted before the file is opened. Run from the REPO ROOT (fixture paths are repo-relative); "-" stands in for the manual's /dev/stdin so the probe does not depend on stdin.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox BAS2-53.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   alpha
   beta
)
a buffer called content is 64 bytes in size.
open a file for writing called output at 1.
open a file for reading called source at each filename from ["-", "docs/ledger/probes/expansion/fixtures/beta.txt"] treating "-" as "docs/ledger/probes/expansion/fixtures/alpha.txt",
  read from source into content,
  write content to output,
  write "\n" to output,
  close source.
close output.
